    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GROVE HOUSE, CORK ROAD, BANDON, CO. CORK \r\nGUIDE PRICE €1.600,000 AMV\r\nFOR SALE\r\n● Spacious two-storey period house for sale on  circa 4.5 acres \r\n● Indoor swimming pool with sauna area\r\n● Walking distance to Bandon town centre\r\n● Master bedroom suite with en-suite bathroom\r\n● Five additional bedrooms\r\n● Short commute to Cork, Macroom & Dunmanway\r\n● Three elegant reception rooms"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ACCOMMODATION\r\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance porch leading to the hallway, downstairs WC, fitted kitchen with breakfast area, utility room, and three reception rooms with access to the garden. Upstairs there are six bedrooms, a family bathroom, and a spacious master suite. Gas central heating."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming period house in a unique setting, located in one of the premier residential areas of Bandon town. The property enjoys a south-facing aspect with stunning views over the town and surrounding countryside. Set in a secluded and private position to the north of the town, the property is\r\napproached via a tree-lined avenue from the public road. The sweeping driveway opens to reveal an impressive and elegant residence.\r\nThe property offers excellent potential as a private family home or, subject to planning permission, a commercial venture. Extending to approximately 4.5 acres, the grounds lead down to a picturesque stream. There is also a large parking area to the front. The property is within a five minutes’ walk of Bandon town and its excellent range of shops and services. Local primary and secondary schools are nearby. Cork city and Cork Airport are within a 30 minutes’ drive via the N71 or R590. Bandon is a historic walled town dating back to the mid-1500s, with many notable buildings and structures. The town also offers a wide range of clubs and societies, while the Bandon River provides scenic leisure walks"
      },
